$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 07/Design recognition

::EPI-W7-001::Participants are grouped by baseline exposure and followed for new disease. What design is this? {
=Cohort study#Correct.
~Case-control study#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Cross-sectional study#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Ecological study#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
}

::EPI-W7-002::Both exposure and outcome have already occurred when records are reviewed, but participants are grouped by earlier exposure. What design is this? {
=Retrospective cohort study#Correct.
~Case-control study#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Cross-sectional study#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Randomised trial#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 07/Incidence and risk

::EPI-W7-003::A cohort observes 20 new cases among 400 exposed and 10 among 500 unexposed. What is the risk ratio? {
=2.50#Correct. Divide risk in exposed by risk in unexposed.
~0.40#Calculate each risk using its own baseline population, then divide.
~2.00#Calculate each risk using its own baseline population, then divide.
~3.00#Calculate each risk using its own baseline population, then divide.
}

