$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 07/Follow-up

::EPI-W7-030::When can loss to follow-up introduce selection bias? {
=When the probability of loss is related to exposure and outcome risk#Correct.
~Whenever exactly one participant is lost#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Only when the sample is small#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Never in cohort studies#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
}

::EPI-W7-031::A participant is disease-free for two years and then moves away. What is the best conceptual treatment of the observed two years? {
=They still contribute observed disease-free person-time before censoring#Correct.
~Treat them as diseased at year two#Observed follow-up can contribute information even if later outcome status is unknown.
~Assume they remained disease-free for the entire planned follow-up#Observed follow-up can contribute information even if later outcome status is unknown.
~Delete all information from them#Observed follow-up can contribute information even if later outcome status is unknown.
}

