$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 07/Comparison

::EPI-W7-041::What is the role of an unexposed comparison cohort? {
=Estimate outcome occurrence expected without the exposure pattern of interest#Correct.
~Guarantee no confounding#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Replace outcome measurement#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Create randomisation#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
}

::EPI-W7-042::Exposed and unexposed workers differ greatly in age before follow-up. What is the main epidemiological concern? {
=Age may confound the exposure-outcome comparison#Correct.
~Cohort design eliminates all baseline differences#Observational cohorts can remain confounded.
~The outcome cannot be measured#Observational cohorts can remain confounded.
~Person-time becomes invalid by definition#Observational cohorts can remain confounded.
}

