$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 07/Interpretation

::EPI-W7-048::Why does a cohort improve temporality compared with a typical cross-sectional study? {
=Exposure can be measured before incident outcome occurs#Correct.
~Cohorts always randomise exposure#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Cohorts cannot have confounding#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
~Cohorts measure only prevalence#Review cohort structure and follow-up.
}

::EPI-W7-049::Why might baseline exposure status be inadequate over long follow-up? {
=Exposure can change over time#Correct.
~Outcomes never occur after baseline#Changing exposure may require time-updated information.
~All cohort studies are retrospective#Changing exposure may require time-updated information.
~Risk ratios require case-control sampling#Changing exposure may require time-updated information.
}

